{
  "name": "Route X mentions to a reply queue, Slack or a log with Apify and OpenAI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "t",
      "name": "Every 4 hours",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        0,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "hours",
              "hoursInterval": 4
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "cfg",
      "name": "What to watch for",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        260,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a1",
              "name": "searchTerms",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "yourbrand"
            },
            {
              "id": "a2",
              "name": "product",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "a note-taking app"
            },
            {
              "id": "a3",
              "name": "maxItems",
              "type": "number",
              "value": 40
            },
            {
              "id": "a4",
              "name": "slackChannel",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "#support-escalations"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "src",
      "name": "Search X",
      "type": "@apify/n8n-nodes-apify.apify",
      "position": [
        520,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "memory": 1024,
        "actorId": "dami_studio~twitter-search-scraper",
        "timeout": 300,
        "resource": "Actors",
        "operation": "Run actor and get dataset",
        "customBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ searchTerms: $json.searchTerms.split(',').map(s => s.trim()), maxItems: $json.maxItems }) }}",
        "maxTotalChargeUsd": 1
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f",
      "name": "Keep mentions worth reading",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.filter",
      "position": [
        780,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 3,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "f1",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ (($json.text || $json.fullText || \"\").toString().length) > 30 }}",
              "rightValue": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.3
    },
    {
      "id": "d",
      "name": "Skip ones already handled",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.removeDuplicates",
      "position": [
        1040,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {
          "scope": "node",
          "historySize": 100000
        },
        "operation": "removeItemsSeenInPreviousExecutions",
        "dedupeValue": "={{ $json.id || $json.url }}"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "llm",
      "name": "Work out what it needs",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "position": [
        1300,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=Someone runs: {{ $('What to watch for').item.json.product }}\n\nRead one public mention of it and decide what, if anything, it needs from them.\n\nMention: {{ ($json.text || $json.fullText || '').toString().slice(0, 1500) }}\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON, no code fence:\n\"route\": exactly one of \"question\", \"complaint\" or \"noise\".\n  - \"question\" when someone is asking something a reply would answer.\n  - \"complaint\" when something is broken or they are unhappy.\n  - \"noise\" for praise, jokes, spam, and anyone just saying the name in passing.\n\"summary\": one sentence on what they want. Empty string for noise.\n\"urgency\": 1 to 5. Only meaningful for complaints; use 1 otherwise.",
        "promptType": "define"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.9
    },
    {
      "id": "model",
      "name": "OpenAI chat model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "position": [
        1300,
        740
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-5-mini"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "sw",
      "name": "Send it where it belongs",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.switch",
      "position": [
        1560,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rules": {
          "values": [
            {
              "outputKey": "Question",
              "conditions": {
                "options": {
                  "version": 2,
                  "leftValue": "",
                  "caseSensitive": true,
                  "typeValidation": "loose"
                },
                "combinator": "and",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "id": "r-Question",
                    "operator": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "operation": "equals"
                    },
                    "leftValue": "={{ JSON.parse($json.text).route }}",
                    "rightValue": "question"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "renameOutput": true
            },
            {
              "outputKey": "Complaint",
              "conditions": {
                "options": {
                  "version": 2,
                  "leftValue": "",
                  "caseSensitive": true,
                  "typeValidation": "loose"
                },
                "combinator": "and",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "id": "r-Complaint",
                    "operator": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "operation": "equals"
                    },
                    "leftValue": "={{ JSON.parse($json.text).route }}",
                    "rightValue": "complaint"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "renameOutput": true
            },
            {
              "outputKey": "Noise",
              "conditions": {
                "options": {
                  "version": 2,
                  "leftValue": "",
                  "caseSensitive": true,
                  "typeValidation": "loose"
                },
                "combinator": "and",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "id": "r-Noise",
                    "operator": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "operation": "equals"
                    },
                    "leftValue": "={{ JSON.parse($json.text).route }}",
                    "rightValue": "noise"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "renameOutput": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.2
    },
    {
      "id": "q",
      "name": "Questions to the reply queue",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.notion",
      "position": [
        1860,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "title": "={{ JSON.parse($json.text).summary }}",
        "options": {},
        "resource": "databasePage",
        "operation": "create",
        "databaseId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        },
        "propertiesUi": {
          "propertyValues": [
            {
              "key": "Link|url",
              "urlValue": "={{ $('Skip ones already handled').item.json.url }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "c",
      "name": "Complaints straight to Slack",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "position": [
        1860,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=:rotating_light: *Complaint* — urgency {{ JSON.parse($json.text).urgency }}/5\n\n{{ JSON.parse($json.text).summary }}\n\n{{ $('Skip ones already handled').item.json.url }}",
        "select": "channel",
        "channelId": "={{ $('What to watch for').first().json.slackChannel }}",
        "otherOptions": {}
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.3
    },
    {
      "id": "n",
      "name": "Everything else just gets logged",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "position": [
        1860,
        740
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "columns": {
          "value": {},
          "mappingMode": "autoMapInputData",
          "matchingColumns": []
        },
        "options": {},
        "operation": "append",
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        },
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.7
    },
    {
      "id": "opt-gmail",
      "name": "Optional: email the questions instead",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "position": [
        700,
        1120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "sendTo": "you@example.com",
        "message": "={{ JSON.parse($json.text).summary }}\n\n{{ $('Skip ones already handled').item.json.url }}",
        "options": {
          "appendAttribution": false
        },
        "subject": "=Someone asked about your product"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "opt-http",
      "name": "Optional: raise a ticket in your helpdesk",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "position": [
        1060,
        1120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://example.com/your-helpdesk",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000
        },
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ summary: JSON.parse($json.text).summary, urgency: JSON.parse($json.text).urgency, url: $('Skip ones already handled').item.json.url }) }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json"
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "st0",
      "name": "Sticky Note s0",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -40,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 1. Schedule\n\nEvery four hours. Someone asking a question in public will not wait for tomorrow."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st1",
      "name": "Sticky Note s1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        220,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 2. What to watch for\n\nThe terms to search and one line describing your product, which is what lets the model tell a real question from a coincidence."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st2",
      "name": "Sticky Note s2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        480,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 3. Search X\n\nPublic mentions only. No X API key."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st3",
      "name": "Sticky Note s3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        740,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 4. Drop the fragments\n\nUnder 30 characters is a mention, not a message."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st4",
      "name": "Sticky Note s4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1000,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 5. Skip repeats\n\nAnything routed in an earlier run never comes round again."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st5",
      "name": "Sticky Note s5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1260,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 6. Work out what it needs\n\nQuestion, complaint or noise — plus a one-line summary and, for complaints, an urgency."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st6",
      "name": "Sticky Note s6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1520,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 7. Send it where it belongs\n\nThree outputs, three destinations. This is the whole point: a complaint and a compliment should not land in the same place."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st7",
      "name": "Sticky Note s7",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1780,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 8. Three endings\n\nQuestions become a reply queue in Notion. Complaints go straight to Slack. Everything else is logged and forgotten."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st-opt",
      "name": "Sticky Note optional",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        660,
        940
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 160,
        "content": "## Optional — other endings\n\nWired to nothing on purpose. Hang **Gmail** off the Question output if you would rather answer from your inbox, or **HTTP Request** off Complaint to open a ticket in whatever helpdesk you use."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st-desc",
      "name": "Sticky Note overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -680,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1500,
        "content": "## Route X mentions to the right place with Apify, OpenAI, Notion and Slack\n\nWatches public mentions of your product and sends each one somewhere different depending on what it actually needs — a reply, an escalation, or nothing at all.\n\n**Who is this for?**\nAnyone whose brand gets mentioned on X often enough that reading every mention is work, but not often enough to justify a social listening tool.\n\n**What problem is this workflow solving?**\nMention alerts treat every mention the same. A person asking whether you support SSO, a person saying your app crashed on launch, and a person using your name in a joke all arrive as the same notification, so you end up reading all of them or none. Almost all of them are noise, and the two that were not get missed.\n\n**What this workflow does**\n- Searches X for your terms every four hours, without an X API key.\n- Drops fragments, and anything routed in an earlier run.\n- Asks a model whether each mention is a question, a complaint or noise, with a one-line summary.\n- Sends each down its own route: questions become a Notion reply queue, complaints go straight to Slack with an urgency, and the rest is logged and forgotten.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Add an Apify credential, an OpenAI credential, plus Notion, Slack and Google Sheets for whichever endings you keep.\n2. Set `searchTerms` and describe your product in one line in \"What to watch for\". That line is what stops the model treating every use of a common word as a mention of you.\n3. Pick your Notion database, Slack channel and sheet in the three ending nodes.\n\n**Requirements**\nAn Apify account and API token, and an OpenAI API key. The destination credentials are only needed for the endings you actually keep — delete the others.\n\n**How to customize this workflow to your needs**\n\nTwo nodes sit below the main row, wired to nothing on purpose. Hang **Gmail** off the Question output to answer from your inbox, or **HTTP Request** off Complaint to open a ticket in your helpdesk.\n\nYou can also delete a whole route. If you only care about complaints, remove the other two endings and the Switch will quietly drop everything else.\n\n**Good to know**\nA brand name that is also an ordinary word will pull in strangers talking about something else entirely, and the product line in the config is the only thing protecting you from that. Make it specific. \"Noise\" is the correct answer for most mentions, and a run where everything routed to noise usually means the search term is too broad, not that the model failed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
